1
00:00:00,059 --> 00:00:01,799
A brick has holes punched straight through

2
00:00:01,839 --> 00:00:03,480
the middle, which is an odd thing to do

3
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:05,319
to an object whose whole job is being solid.

4
00:00:05,559 --> 00:00:06,539
The holes make it better.

5
00:00:06,839 --> 00:00:08,819
Mortar squeezes down into them and sets there,

6
00:00:09,099 --> 00:00:10,679
so each brick is keyed into the one above

7
00:00:10,939 --> 00:00:12,539
rather than glued along a flat face.

8
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:15,339
Wet clay also has to dry and fire without

9
00:00:15,399 --> 00:00:17,159
cracking, and heat reaches the middle of a

10
00:00:17,239 --> 00:00:19,399
perforated brick far faster than a solid lump.

11
00:00:19,719 --> 00:00:20,899
Less clay, less fuel,

12
00:00:21,219 --> 00:00:22,759
lighter to lift, stronger wall.
